id: pm-tl7vlu
title: "GH-1530: dependency advisory CLI silently skips checks through filesystem aliases"
description: "MacOS nightly39575255547 on main2a1e7dab0 fails parsing empty stdout from the copied dependency advisory executable. The executable compares lexical argv[1] against canonical import.meta.url. A Linux symlink reproduction of the exact script returns exit0 and empty output even for --unknown, confirming silent entrypoint bypass. Resolve physical script identity before deciding whether to execute; retain side-effect-free imports."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,macos,nightly,read-output,security
created_at: "2026-10-21T09:48:44.974Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T10:44:21.930Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T10:39:28.621Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T10:39:28.621Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "Real and aliased executable paths emit the complete verified receipt and reject invalid arguments; importing the module does not execute the gate; unchanged-source alias regression fails before and passes after the fix; supported hosted macOS verification runs without weakening advisory, coverage or timeout policies"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Canonicalize invocation and module paths before executing advisory verification; cover real and aliased paths in ordinary and symlink-preserving Node modes, preserve inert imports, and register the advisory recurrence family."
expected_result: "Alias spelling cannot suppress dependency checks: successful invocations emit complete verified receipts, invalid arguments fail, imports stay inert, and native macOS verifies the same behavior."
actual_result: "The unchanged alias test failed before the fix with empty JSON output; all22 advisory and8 policy tests now pass, both hosted macOS Node24 shards passed, and complete lineage validation reports zero uncovered members. Final PR checks remain mandatory before merge."
